OL,3,GNEWSACracks in bridge force extended
OL,4,Alane closure
OL,5,
OL,6,FCracks in the deck of a bridge that
OL,7,Fprovides one of the main routes for
OL,8,Fdrivers in and out of a city have been
OL,9,Fdiscovered, engineers have said.
OL,11,FOne lane on Bridge Road, near Countess
OL,12,FWear, Exeter, has been closed for a
OL,13,Fweek and that closure is now being
OL,14,Fextended for engineers to carry out
OL,15,Frepair works.
OL,17,FDevon County Council engineer Simon
OL,18,FHill said: "We've got an aluminium deck
OL,19,Fthat is starting to corrode and break
OL,20,Fup and is no longer supported
OL,21,Funderneath."
OL,23,APub: 28-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
